From 08a92986d546236ed4ed4e35afa219efd2929b38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tatsuki Tanaka <tatsuki@tanakatatsuki.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:40:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/46] ASoC: codecs: aw88261: add support for AW88263S
 amplifier

Add support for the Awinic AW88263S smart audio amplifier:
- Hardware mute bit inversion and TX enable handling
- Proper volume bit-shift (6-bit range) and VCALB 0x56 calibration
- Asynchronous startup with robust PLL lock verification
- Continuous amplifier retry loop to handle early playback clock jitter

Signed-off-by: Tatsuki Tanaka <tatsuki@tanakatatsuki.dev>
(cherry picked from commit 814f45037c1d933048349daa0ef17b074593f9c0)

Conflict resolution for Linux 7.3: 7.3 converted aw88261_playback_event() to guard(mutex); the commit's per-case locking (the delayed start work must not run under the lock held across cancel_delayed_work_sync()) replaces the function-wide guard.
